The original [incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) claims one known issue with one queued fix. The exported data and running components show separate causes. A shared subject does not prove a shared problem.

## Engineering outcome — 5 October 2026

The course's engineering update reports #4471 closed on 5 October. The parser is **fixed**: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The hint is **won't fix** because the `booking-v3` form was retired. These are different closure reasons. Retirement does not establish that the hint was corrected.

The public tracking issues are [parser, completed](https://github.com/szymonkm/mega-s01e03/issues/1) and [hint, not planned](https://github.com/szymonkm/mega-s01e03/issues/2). Historical report counts remain tied to the export. The sections below explain the original symptoms and required checks.

## Count the reports, then classify

<ReviewSummary />

Use `uniqueById` before filtering `mergedInto === 4471`. Then use `groupByCause` with `tenantOf`. These functions read the tenant directory and use the platform's date-field order. Counts below are computed from the export, not copied from the old page.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Parser problem

The shared parser reads month first. Day-first tenants therefore get swapped dates. This affects app and email reports, plus forms whose hints agree with their tenant's date order.

For example, report `R-41200` from `harbour.dental` describes an April booking appearing in July. Report `R-41205` belongs here despite its `hint` intake tag: `morrow.tax` uses a day-first locale and this report came through the app.

Fix the parser's date contract. Use an explicit date format or structured date fields. Verify ambiguous and unambiguous dates against each tenant's locale.

## Form-hint problem

The `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` for day-first tenants. People follow that hint, but the form interprets their entry in the tenant's order. This is a separate bug and needs a separate fix.

Reports come through the form for `alder.physio`, `copper.studio`, and `pale.harbour`. Report `R-41230` belongs here despite its `parser` intake tag. Fix the displayed hint and make its format agree with the input interpretation. Test all affected tenant configurations.

## What the timeline shows

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Compare receipt dates with merge dates. The July merge spike records desk activity; it does not show that the problem started in July. Reports continued after the first merge. Marking the ticket known did not stop the reports.

## Change how the desk merges reports

The [old subject rule](/kb/triage/dedupe) can merge different causes and split one cause across different subjects. Its review date is old enough to trigger the kb's stale-page warning. Read the [replacement decision](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) before merging more reports.

Use tenant locale, form version, channel, and symptom evidence. If the cause is unknown, keep the report separate until reviewed. Check new reports against the parser fix and form retirement before merging them into this closed incident. Keep the accepted historical decision unchanged.

## Evidence and limits

This review uses the 2026-10-04 export: `reports-4471.json`, the tenant directory, `desk-notes.json`, and the supplied classification and chart components. Closure outcomes come from the engineering update on the course challenge page, checked on 2026-10-31. The export itself predates that update. New reports can change the counts. Rebuild this page after replacing an export.

